\subsection{Superintendent Turnover}

Superintendent turnover models are slightly different in that they are logistic 
regression models predicting a binary outcome of whether the superintendent 
turned over or not. Table \ref{tab:supMod} shows the results of these logistic 
regressions. Here, incumbent defeat is consistently positively related with 
superintendent turnover, but this effect is only statistically significant in 
the first model. The estimated effect is quite large -- an incumbent defeat 
translates into an odds-ratio of 1.31. 

<<newSup, results='asis'>>=
modeldata <- dist_turn[, c("distid", "year", "incsDefeated", "servingMembers",
                           "MATH_PROFADV_PER", "NEW_SUP", "SUP_EXPERIENCE",
                           "econ_disadv_per", "VAP_adj", "per65o", 
                           "challengRate", "dissatFactor",
                           "PerBachelorOrAbove", "locale2")]
modeldata$incsDefeatedFac <- ifelse(modeldata$incsDefeated > 0, 1, 0)
modeldata$incsDefeatedFac <- factor(modeldata$incsDefeatedFac)
preTreat <- modeldata[modeldata$year <= 2010,]
preTreat$year <- preTreat$year + 2
names(preTreat) <- paste(names(preTreat), "lag", sep = "_")
modeldata <- modeldata[, c("NEW_SUP", "distid", "year")]
modeldata <- merge(modeldata, preTreat, by.y = c("distid_lag", "year_lag"), 
                 by.x = c("distid", "year"))
modeldata <- modeldata[modeldata$year > 2005, ]
modeldata$SUP_EXPERIENCE_lag <- ifelse(is.na(modeldata$SUP_EXPERIENCE_lag), 0, 
                                       modeldata$SUP_EXPERIENCE_lag)

simpModSup <- glm(NEW_SUP ~ incsDefeatedFac_lag + locale2_lag + 
                    servingMembers_lag + log(VAP_adj_lag), 
                  data = modeldata, family = "binomial")
simpModSup$se <- sqrt(diag(get_CL_vcov(simpModSup, modeldata$distid)))
fullModSup <- glm(NEW_SUP ~ incsDefeatedFac_lag + econ_disadv_per_lag + 
                   log(VAP_adj_lag) + servingMembers_lag + NEW_SUP_lag +
                    locale2_lag + PerBachelorOrAbove_lag + 
                   per65o_lag, data = modeldata, family = "binomial")
fullModSup$se <- sqrt(diag(get_CL_vcov(fullModSup, modeldata$distid)))
library(arm)
fullModSupFE <- bayesglm(NEW_SUP ~ incsDefeatedFac_lag + 
                      econ_disadv_per_lag + log(VAP_adj_lag) + servingMembers_lag +
                      locale2_lag + PerBachelorOrAbove_lag + 
                   per65o_lag + distid, data = modeldata, family = "binomial")
fullModSupFE$se <- sqrt(diag(get_CL_vcov(fullModSupFE, modeldata$distid)))
prettyNames <- c("Intercept", "Inc. Def. Lag", "Exurb", "Rural", "Board Size",
                  "ln(VAP)", "FRL \\%", "New Sup. Lag", "\\% Bach. +", 
                 "\\% Over 65")

fe.note <- "District fixed effects not displayed."

apsrtable(simpModSup, fullModSup, fullModSupFE, se = "robust", 
          stars = "default", digits = 3, 
          model.names = c("Simple", "Lag", "FE"), 
          caption = "Incumbent Defeat and Superintendent Turnover", 
          label = "tab:supMod", notes = list(stars.note, fe.note), 
          Sweave = FALSE, 
           omitcoef=list("distid", 
                         expression(grep("distid", coefnames, value=TRUE))), 
          coef.names = prettyNames, size = "small")

@

<<chalRateGrad, results='asis'>>=


simpModSupc <- update(simpModSup, . ~ challengRate_lag + . - incsDefeatedFac_lag)
simpModSupc$se <- sqrt(diag(get_CL_vcov(simpModSupc, modeldata$distid)))
fullModSupc <- update(fullModSup, . ~ challengRate_lag + . - incsDefeatedFac_lag)
fullModSupc$se <- sqrt(diag(get_CL_vcov(fullModSupc, modeldata$distid)))
fullModSupFEc <- update(fullModSupFE, . ~ challengRate_lag + . - incsDefeatedFac_lag)
fullModSupFEc$se <- sqrt(diag(get_CL_vcov(fullModSupFEc, modeldata$distid)))

prettyNames <- c("Intercept", "Challenge Rate", "Exurb", "Rural", "Board Size",
                  "ln(VAP)", "FRL \\%", "New Sup. Lag", "\\% Bach. +", 
                 "\\% Over 65")

apsrtable(simpModSupc, fullModSupc, fullModSupFEc, se = "robust", 
          stars = "default", digits = 3, 
          model.names = c("Simple", "Lag", "FE"), 
          caption = "Challenge Rate and Superintendent Turnover", 
          label = "tab:supMod2", notes = list(stars.note, fe.note), 
          Sweave = FALSE, 
           omitcoef=list("distid", 
                         expression(grep("distid", coefnames, value=TRUE))), 
          coef.names = prettyNames, size = "small")
@

<<dissatFatGrad, results='asis'>>=
simpModSupd <- update(simpModSupc, . ~ dissatFactor_lag + . - challengRate_lag)
simpModSupd$se <- sqrt(diag(get_CL_vcov(simpModSupc, modeldata$distid)))
fullModSupd <- update(fullModSupc, . ~ dissatFactor_lag + . - challengRate_lag)
fullModSupd$se <- sqrt(diag(get_CL_vcov(fullModSupc, modeldata$distid)))
fullModSupFEd <- update(fullModSupFEc, . ~ dissatFactor_lag + . - challengRate_lag)
fullModSupFEd$se <- sqrt(diag(get_CL_vcov(fullModSupFEc, modeldata$distid)))

prettyNames <- c("Intercept", "Dissat. Factor", "Exurb", "Rural", "Board Size",
                  "ln(VAP)", "FRL \\%", "New Sup. Lag", "\\% Bach. +", 
                 "\\% Over 65")

apsrtable(simpModSupd, fullModSupd, fullModSupFEd, se = "robust", 
          stars = "default", digits = 3, 
          model.names = c("Simple", "Lag", "FE"), 
          caption = "Dissatisfaction Factor and Superintendent Turnover", 
          label = "tab:supMod3", notes = list(stars.note, fe.note), 
          Sweave = FALSE, 
           omitcoef=list("distid", 
                         expression(grep("distid", coefnames, value=TRUE))), 
          coef.names = prettyNames, size = "small")

@

Another interesting effect that emerges from the models in Table \ref{tab:supMod} 
is a consistently statistically significant and positive effect on the size of a 
school board on the likelihood of a superintendent being removed. A board with 
an increased size of 1 is associated with a 14\% increase in the likelihood of 
a superintendent changing. This effect stays statistically significant and 
roughly the same size across the specifications of the model. 

\clearpage

\section{Conclusion}

Counter to the prior findings in the literature, this chapter has looked for 
evidence of an impact of school board incumbent defeat on student outcomes and 
district policy and found little. 

\citet{RefWorks:246} finds that board dissatisfaction does lead to superintendent 
turnover. 

This chapter has looked for evidence of the impact of school board electoral 
defeat on student outcomes and on school district leadership. 

